Hey, how's it going?


00:07:15.268 --> 00:07:16.611
Mmm, just working.


00:07:18.063 --> 00:07:20.031
Taking a break from avoiding the show.


00:07:25.362 --> 00:07:28.912
So, you still toiling away at the hospice?


00:07:29.658 --> 00:07:32.036
Yeah, between this and the, uh, preschool.


00:07:34.162 --> 00:07:36.962
So what's our deadline now? Seven months?


00:07:37.707 --> 00:07:40.335
- Six and a half.
- Ooh, coming up.


00:07:42.003 --> 00:07:43.550
Any ideas for titles?


00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:52.602
Come in.


00:07:53.765 --> 00:07:54.857
Hey...


00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.602
- Good night, kiddo.
- Good night.


00:07:59.562 --> 00:08:00.484
Are you, uh...


00:08:00.897 --> 00:08:02.900
Are you feeling okay about everything?


00:08:03.233 --> 00:08:04.655
Yeah. Fine.


00:08:05.902 --> 00:08:06.903
A little sad?


00:08:07.696 --> 00:08:09.994
Mmm...


00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:11.787
Yeah, I get it.


00:08:12.659 --> 00:08:13.501
I know.


00:08:14.285 --> 00:08:15.537
- Good night.
- Night.


00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:16.621
Love you.


00:08:32.387 --> 00:08:33.229
Who's this?


00:08:36.057 --> 00:08:37.058
That's Grandma?


00:08:48.361 --> 00:08:50.159
You know you were her favorite, right?


00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:53.787
Even when you were a little baby,


00:08:53.867 --> 00:08:56.120
she wouldn't let me feed you
because she needed to feed you.


00:08:56.369 --> 00:08:57.621
Drove me crazy.


00:08:58.997 --> 00:09:00.795
She wanted me to be a boy.


00:09:05.628 --> 00:09:07.631
You know, I was a tomboy
when I was growing up.


00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.473
I hated dresses and dolls and pink.


00:09:14.596 --> 00:09:16.189
Who's gonna take care of me?


00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:19.601
Um, excuse me.


00:09:19.684 --> 00:09:21.436
You don't think I'm gonna take care of you?


00:09:23.146 --> 00:09:24.523
But when you die.


00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:28.526
Well, then...


00:09:30.111 --> 00:09:31.408
Dad will take care of you.


00:09:32.947 --> 00:09:33.789
Or Peter.


00:09:51.132 --> 00:09:52.759
You never cried as a baby.


00:09:54.844 --> 00:09:55.720
You know that?


00:09:58.056 --> 00:09:59.399
Even when you were born.


00:10:08.817 --> 00:10:10.490
Did you feel like you wanted to cry today?


00:10:16.074 --> 00:10:17.576
You think it might feel like a relief?


00:10:43.518 --> 00:10:44.519
Good night, sweetheart.


00:12:37.298 --> 00:12:38.174
Mom?


00:13:19.507 --> 00:13:21.430
I just scared myself in the workshop.


00:13:22.802 --> 00:13:24.270
With... With what?


00:13:29.767 --> 00:13:30.814
No.


00:13:52.749 --> 00:13:53.716
Are you done?


00:13:55.752 --> 00:13:56.753
Almost.


00:13:58.421 --> 00:14:01.266
So, maybe we finish the toy after the quiz.


00:14:01.591 --> 00:14:02.467
What do you think?


00:14:05.094 --> 00:14:06.141
- Okay.
- Okay.


00:14:15.188 --> 00:14:17.360
Oh, my God! What was that?


00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:36.001
So, if we go by the rule
that the hero is undone by his fatal flaw,


00:14:36.084 --> 00:14:38.462
what is Heracles' flaw?


00:14:39.962 --> 00:14:40.963
Arrogance.


00:14:41.214 --> 00:14:42.341
Okay.


00:14:42.757 --> 00:14:43.599
Why?


00:14:44.133 --> 00:14:46.931
Because he literally refuses
to look at all the signs


00:14:47.011 --> 00:14:49.765
that are being literally
handed to him the entire play.


00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:52.518
Okay, interesting.


00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.443
So he thinks he has control.


00:14:54.936 --> 00:14:59.485
But let's all remember, Sophocles wrote
the oracle so that it was unconditional,


00:14:59.565 --> 00:15:03.531
meaning, Heracles never had
any choice, right?


00:15:03.611 --> 00:15:06.534
So does that make it
more tragic or less tragic


00:15:06.614 --> 00:15:08.786
that if he has a choice?


00:15:08.866 --> 00:15:10.664
- Less.
- Okay.


00:15:10.993 --> 00:15:12.540
- Why?
- Because.


00:15:15.665 --> 00:15:17.167
Care to weigh in, Peter?


00:15:19.085 --> 00:15:20.837
Um, about which part?


00:15:23.339 --> 00:15:26.387
I think it's more tragic because,
if it's all just inevitable,


00:15:26.467 --> 00:15:28.431
then that means that
the characters had no hope.


00:15:28.511 --> 00:15:31.389
They never had hope because
they're all just, like, hopeless.


00:15:31.472 --> 00:15:34.772
They're all like pawns
in this horrible, hopeless machine.


00:16:48.966 --> 00:16:50.639
- Hello!
- Hi!


00:17:33.469 --> 00:17:34.687
Did you go up in my mom's room?


00:17:36.222 --> 00:17:37.189
No.


00:17:38.057 --> 00:17:39.650
Mmm. Door was open.


00:17:46.023 --> 00:17:46.899
Hello?


00:17:46.983 --> 00:17:48.529
Sorry. I know it's irrational.


00:17:48.609 --> 00:17:49.781
- No problem.
- Thank you.


00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:53.038
Hey, Dad. It's the cemetery.


00:17:53.823 --> 00:17:54.699
About what?


00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:56.576
Let me see.


00:17:57.618 --> 00:17:58.460
Hello?


00:17:59.537 --> 00:18:00.379
Yes.


00:18:07.712 --> 00:18:08.713
What does that mean?


00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:10.881
Desecrated?


00:18:15.845 --> 00:18:17.188
But it's only been a week.


00:18:20.933 --> 00:18:23.436
Yes, okay, yes. Sure.


00:18:24.145 --> 00:18:25.942
All right. I understand. Yes...


00:18:26.022 --> 00:18:28.275
Uh, why don't I call you back? Yes. Goodbye.


00:18:28.357 --> 00:18:29.404
What was it?


00:18:31.569 --> 00:18:33.572
Uh, just some billing crap.


00:18:35.323 --> 00:18:37.291
Okay, well, I'm, uh...
I'm gonna go see a movie.


00:18:38.701 --> 00:18:39.577
Okay.


00:19:07.104 --> 00:19:08.317
He would say,


00:19:08.397 --> 00:19:11.116
"I'm a burden, I'm a burden, I'm a burden."


00:19:15.404 --> 00:19:17.623
And I would tell him, "No, no."


00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:27.424
But yes, he was a burden.


00:19:28.417 --> 00:19:31.591
Now we've set aside
some time for any newcomers


00:19:31.671 --> 00:19:32.843
who might like to speak.


00:19:33.506 --> 00:19:35.052
So, anyone.


00:19:35.132 --> 00:19:39.604
If it's your first or second time with us,
the floor is open.


00:19:43.974 --> 00:19:46.728
Yes. Would you like to...


00:19:46.811 --> 00:19:47.733
Maybe not.


00:19:48.646 --> 00:19:49.568
Okay.


00:19:50.398 --> 00:19:51.240
No pressure.


00:19:59.073 --> 00:19:59.995
My name's Annie.


00:20:00.449 --> 00:20:01.621
Hi, Annie.


00:20:03.494 --> 00:20:05.041
My mom died a week ago.


00:20:05.663 --> 00:20:06.835
So I'm just here for...


00:20:07.832 --> 00:20:08.674
trying it.


00:20:09.917 --> 00:20:11.920
I have a lot of resistance
to things like this,


00:20:12.545 --> 00:20:15.549
but I came to these a couple years ago.


00:20:15.631 --> 00:20:18.476
Well, I was forced to come
and I guess it, um...


00:20:20.219 --> 00:20:21.721
I guess it helped. So, um...


00:20:25.057 --> 00:20:28.277
My mom was old, and she wasn't
all together there at the end.


00:20:28.686 --> 00:20:33.316
And we were pretty much estranged before
that, so it really wasn't a huge blow.


00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:36.277
But I did...


00:20:38.404 --> 00:20:39.280
love her.


00:20:41.031 --> 00:20:42.408
And she didn't have an easy life.


00:20:42.491 --> 00:20:45.119
She had DID, which became extreme at the end.


00:20:45.911 --> 00:20:46.833
And dementia.


00:20:47.496 --> 00:20:51.217
And my father died
when I was a baby from starvation,


00:20:51.584 --> 00:20:55.383
um, because he had psychotic
depression and he starved himself,


00:20:55.463 --> 00:20:57.510
which I'm sure
was just as pleasant as it sounds.


00:20:57.590 --> 00:20:58.682
And then there's my brother.


00:20:59.216 --> 00:21:01.138
My older brother had schizophrenia,


00:21:01.218 --> 00:21:04.183
and when he was 16, he hanged
himself in my mother's bedroom


00:21:04.263 --> 00:21:06.102
and of course his suicide note blamed her,


00:21:06.182 --> 00:21:09.231
accusing her of putting people
inside him. So...


00:21:12.938 --> 00:21:14.611
That was my mom's life.


00:21:27.453 --> 00:21:30.292
And then she lived in our house
at the end, before hospice.


00:21:30.372 --> 00:21:31.999
We weren't even talking before that.


00:21:32.082 --> 00:21:33.629
I mean, we were, and then we weren't.


00:21:34.376 --> 00:21:35.343
And then we were.


00:21:38.839 --> 00:21:40.428
She's completely manipulative.


00:21:40.508 --> 00:21:43.723
Until my husband finally enforced
a no-contact rule,


00:21:43.803 --> 00:21:45.771
which lasted until I got pregnant
with my daughter.


00:21:46.222 --> 00:21:48.936
I didn't let her anywhere near me
when I had my first, my son,


00:21:49.016 --> 00:21:50.855
which is why I gave her my daughter,


00:21:50.935 --> 00:21:52.983
who she immediately stabbed her hooks into.


00:21:53.729 --> 00:21:56.068
And I just... I felt guilty again.


00:21:56.148 --> 00:21:57.491
I felt guilty again.


00:21:58.192 --> 00:21:59.238
When she got sick,


00:21:59.318 --> 00:22:01.571
not that she was really even
my mom at the end,


00:22:01.654 --> 00:22:05.875
and not that she would
ever feel guilty about anything.


00:22:10.746 --> 00:22:13.966
And I just don't want to put
any more stress on my family.


00:22:16.544 --> 00:22:18.296
I'm not even really sure if they could...


00:22:20.506 --> 00:22:21.758
Could give me that support.


00:22:25.803 --> 00:22:27.021
And I just... I just feel like...


00:22:31.183 --> 00:22:32.981
I just sometimes feel like it's all ruined.


00:22:36.021 --> 00:22:37.398
And then I realize


00:22:38.524 --> 00:22:39.992
that I am to blame.


00:22:42.778 --> 00:22:44.246
Or not that I'm to blame,


00:22:46.615 --> 00:22:48.458
but I am blamed! I'm...


00:22:49.869 --> 00:22:53.214
And what do you think you feel blamed for?


00:22:56.917 --> 00:22:57.918
I don't know.


00:23:02.256 --> 00:23:04.133
<i>Hey, what's going on in town anyway, mister?</i>


00:23:04.216 --> 00:23:05.262
<i>A convention or something?</i>


00:23:05.342 --> 00:23:06.263
<i>What?</i>


00:23:06.343 --> 00:23:07.515
<i>Those clothes you're wearing.</i>


00:23:07.595 --> 00:23:09.848
<i>I talked to a guy this morning
who was wearing the same kind of outfit.</i>


00:23:10.222 --> 00:23:11.940
<i>Maybe the guy you're looking for, huh?</i>


00:23:12.391 --> 00:23:13.438
<i>You spoke to him?</i>


00:23:14.268 --> 00:23:16.145
<i>What did he tell you? Where did he go?</i>


00:23:16.228 --> 00:23:17.441
<i>Hey, what's the matter with you?</i>


00:23:17.521 --> 00:23:18.898
<i>Hey, take your hands off me.</i>


00:23:18.981 --> 00:23:20.277
<i>You will tell me what he said to you!</i>


00:23:20.357 --> 00:23:22.780
<i>Well, why should I?
Hey, who do you think you are anyway?</i>


00:23:25.112 --> 00:23:26.700
<i>He came in with the dog tags!</i>


00:23:26.780 --> 00:23:28.744
<i>Wanted to know about the address
and I told him how to find it.</i>


00:23:28.824 --> 00:23:29.746
<i>Where?</i>


00:25:35.242 --> 00:25:36.539
Hey, um,


00:25:37.369 --> 00:25:40.088
do you think I could maybe borrow
one of the cars tonight?


00:25:40.205 --> 00:25:43.004
Why? Where are you going?


00:25:43.333 --> 00:25:45.631
Oh, just like a school barbecue thing.


00:25:46.253 --> 00:25:47.630
Oh, so you're not eating with us?


00:25:48.130 --> 00:25:49.677
No, I was still gonna eat here.


00:25:49.923 --> 00:25:51.387
Well, you can eat there
if you want. I just didn't...


00:25:51.467 --> 00:25:53.806
No, no, no. I'm gonna eat here.
I just... I...


00:25:53.886 --> 00:25:56.435
Just be going to hang out.


00:25:59.391 --> 00:26:00.438
No drinking?


00:26:02.186 --> 00:26:04.860
We're not even old enough
to get drinks if we wanted to.


00:26:05.481 --> 00:26:07.905
Well, that's a crock.
I'm just asking if you're drinking.


00:26:08.734 --> 00:26:10.111
Well, I just answered no.


00:26:12.154 --> 00:26:13.531
You gonna take your sister?


00:26:15.365 --> 00:26:17.959
Uh... Does she want to go?


00:26:18.786 --> 00:26:21.210
Have you asked her?


00:26:25.125 --> 00:26:26.126
Charlie?


00:26:56.657 --> 00:26:57.499
Charlie!


00:26:59.868 --> 00:27:03.919
I mean, what are you doing?
Leaving the house barefoot?


00:27:04.414 --> 00:27:05.627
Are you some kind of idiot?


00:27:05.707 --> 00:27:07.755
You can't roam around
with no shoes and no coat.


00:27:08.210 --> 00:27:09.678
- I want Grandma.
- Oh.


00:27:10.629 --> 00:27:12.848
Oh, what? You're angry with me now?


00:27:16.593 --> 00:27:18.721
You are going to this... Hey, socks off.


00:27:19.138 --> 00:27:20.685
You're going to this party with your brother.


00:27:21.640 --> 00:27:22.641
What party?


00:27:22.724 --> 00:27:25.068
Some school hangout with other kids.


00:27:26.687 --> 00:27:27.563
That's okay.


00:27:27.646 --> 00:27:30.149
No, it's not okay. You're going.


00:27:30.732 --> 00:27:32.529
- Why?
- Because it'll be fun.


00:27:32.609 --> 00:27:34.156
Because you'll get to hang out
with other kids.


00:27:34.236 --> 00:27:35.574
- With who?
- With your...


00:27:35.654 --> 00:27:37.201
With your brother. With other kids.


00:27:42.703 --> 00:27:44.205
- Fine.
- Good. You're going.


00:27:44.288 --> 00:27:46.006
- She's going with you.
- Great.


00:27:46.290 --> 00:27:47.837
Now this really means no drinking.


00:27:48.250 --> 00:27:49.843
Yeah, I really wasn't going to.


00:29:26.431 --> 00:29:27.683
<i>Whoa. Hi.</i>


00:29:29.226 --> 00:29:30.342
Oh. Hi.


00:29:31.228 --> 00:29:32.195
How's the party?


00:29:33.814 --> 00:29:35.612
Why? You wanna know if you should come?


00:29:36.358 --> 00:29:38.076
Uh, yeah. What do ya think?


00:29:40.862 --> 00:29:41.829
Either way.


00:29:44.908 --> 00:29:46.410
Hey, do you happen to smoke at all?


00:29:47.119 --> 00:29:48.792
I have really good weed.


00:29:55.127 --> 00:29:57.380
- The other room has a bong.
- Sick.


00:30:03.010 --> 00:30:04.556
Do you wanna wait out here for a second?


00:30:04.636 --> 00:30:06.725
- No.
- Charlie, please, just...


00:30:06.805 --> 00:30:08.557
It'll be two minutes
and then we can hang out.


00:30:08.640 --> 00:30:09.516
You can draw.


00:30:10.100 --> 00:30:11.318
Please, Charlie. I'm...


00:30:13.312 --> 00:30:15.189
Oh, shit, look.
They're giving out chocolate cake.


00:30:15.272 --> 00:30:16.524
Not to everyone.


00:30:16.606 --> 00:30:17.778
Yes, to everyone. It's a party.


00:30:17.858 --> 00:30:19.905
- I don't know anyone.
- Nobody does.


00:30:19.985 --> 00:30:22.488
Just walk over and stand there
and they'll give you a piece.


00:30:22.821 --> 00:30:24.323
Hurry up. They're gonna run out.
Come on, Charlie.


00:30:30.495 --> 00:30:31.337
Hey, guys.


00:30:32.914 --> 00:30:33.790
Peter has weed.


00:30:57.856 --> 00:30:59.278
That was your sister downstairs?


00:30:59.733 --> 00:31:01.736
Yeah. Charlie.


00:31:03.695 --> 00:31:04.742
Is your sister hot?


00:31:07.866 --> 00:31:09.459
I actually saw her drawing me last week.


00:31:09.910 --> 00:31:10.831
Oh, yeah?


00:31:10.911 --> 00:31:13.130
Yeah. She made me look retarded.


00:31:13.955 --> 00:31:15.127
Yeah. That's Charlie.


00:31:44.861 --> 00:31:45.828
Peter?


00:31:46.446 --> 00:31:48.164
Charlie.


00:31:49.491 --> 00:31:51.459
What's up?


00:31:56.289 --> 00:31:57.165
Are you okay?


00:31:59.084 --> 00:32:00.586
It's hard to breathe.


00:32:02.671 --> 00:32:03.547
What do you mean?


00:32:04.840 --> 00:32:07.059
I think my throat's getting bigger.


00:32:56.433 --> 00:32:58.356
It's okay, Charlie.
We're almost at the hospital, okay?


00:33:17.787 --> 00:33:18.754
Charlie!


00:34:38.535 --> 00:34:39.536
Okay.


00:34:42.789 --> 00:34:43.756
Okay.


00:35:52.359 --> 00:35:54.077
Okay, good. They're home.


00:35:54.986 --> 00:35:56.033
Good.


00:36:53.628 --> 00:36:55.130
I'm running out for some balsam wood.


00:36:55.213 --> 00:36:56.260
You want anything?


00:36:56.548 --> 00:36:58.642
I'm good, sweetheart. Drive safe.


00:36:58.967 --> 00:36:59.934
Okay.


00:37:00.677 --> 00:37:01.804
Back in 20.


00:37:39.299 --> 00:37:42.428
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!


00:37:47.599 --> 00:37:50.978
Oh, no. I can't, I can't...


00:37:51.770 --> 00:37:54.319
I just want to die!


00:38:03.156 --> 00:38:05.784
Oh, God. It hurts too much!


00:38:05.867 --> 00:38:07.790
I just need to die!


00:38:12.624 --> 00:38:15.673
Charlie!


00:38:20.089 --> 00:38:23.309
Oh, God.


00:38:29.974 --> 00:38:32.523
Oh, Charlie!


00:42:05.773 --> 00:42:08.117
Hey, are you guys friends
with Becky on Facebook?


00:42:09.027 --> 00:42:10.529
You're friends with Becky?


00:42:11.112 --> 00:42:13.536
Dude, I said "Facebook friends."


00:42:14.782 --> 00:42:16.534
But seriously, you see her statuses, bro?


00:42:16.617 --> 00:42:18.331
Oh, my God, dude, I know.


00:42:18.411 --> 00:42:20.038
- Like, every ten seconds.
- For real.


00:42:20.663 --> 00:42:24.042
Oh, dude, what about, uh, fucking...
Let me hit that.


00:42:24.667 --> 00:42:26.631
- Brian?
- Brian and his girlfriend.


00:42:26.711 --> 00:42:28.043
He calls her something...


00:42:28.129 --> 00:42:30.093
He calls her something really goofy, dude.
What does he...


00:42:30.173 --> 00:42:31.300
Oh, he calls her "princess."


00:42:34.010 --> 00:42:36.099
Who fucking calls
their girlfriend "princess"?


00:42:36.179 --> 00:42:37.431
What the fuck?


00:42:37.680 --> 00:42:38.726
Dude, he's like,


00:42:38.806 --> 00:42:41.604
"I'm picking up my princess
from the airport."


00:42:41.684 --> 00:42:43.606
Fucking eating cous... What the fuck.


00:42:43.686 --> 00:42:44.649
It's couscous.


00:42:44.729 --> 00:42:46.902
Couscous. I don't give a shit.
"...with my princess."


00:42:47.690 --> 00:42:49.112
You hit that shit?


00:42:49.192 --> 00:42:50.238
Who's his girlfriend?


00:42:50.318 --> 00:42:53.697
Some, uh, some fucking stupid college chick.


00:42:54.989 --> 00:42:55.827
Oh, damn.


00:42:55.907 --> 00:42:58.496
I wanna fucking stupid college princess, bro.


00:42:58.576 --> 00:43:00.123
Yeah.


00:43:00.203 --> 00:43:03.126
Oh, hey, dude. Dude, dude, dude.
Are you... Are you all right?


00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:08.094
I think I'm having a... Like a reaction.


00:43:08.628 --> 00:43:10.130
- What?
- My throat is...


00:43:10.213 --> 00:43:11.635
I think my throat is getting bigger.


00:43:12.507 --> 00:43:14.851
Dude, it's just... It's just weed.


00:43:15.843 --> 00:43:17.095
Chill, man. It's all right.


00:43:17.762 --> 00:43:19.139
Just hold my hand. Hold on.


00:44:56.402 --> 00:44:59.742
Uh, I'm so sorry to chase you down.


00:44:59.822 --> 00:45:02.200
Uh, were you not coming in, or...


00:45:03.159 --> 00:45:06.833
I... No, I just, um... I forgot something.


00:45:06.913 --> 00:45:09.377
Oh, okay, sorry. Sorry, I just...


00:45:09.457 --> 00:45:11.630
I recognized you from a few months ago.


00:45:12.877 --> 00:45:16.222
Oh, God. I feel very silly. I'm Joan.


00:45:17.840 --> 00:45:18.716
Hi.


00:45:19.258 --> 00:45:20.601
Are you doing better?


00:45:22.053 --> 00:45:22.895
What?


00:45:23.304 --> 00:45:24.305
After your mother?


00:45:25.264 --> 00:45:27.642
What? No, no. That's not...


00:45:30.269 --> 00:45:32.863
My, um... My daughter was killed.


00:45:33.564 --> 00:45:34.531
Oh.


00:45:34.857 --> 00:45:36.825
I'm...


00:45:36.984 --> 00:45:39.237
I'm so, so sorry.


00:45:40.529 --> 00:45:43.078
Oh, would you like to come in with me?


00:45:43.407 --> 00:45:45.329
Or we could even just have a coffee.


00:45:45.409 --> 00:45:47.707
Uh, I'm sorry. Really, I, um...


00:45:48.162 --> 00:45:50.665
I can't... I really did forget something.


00:45:50.748 --> 00:45:51.920
My son died.


00:45:54.001 --> 00:45:54.968
Oh.


00:45:58.089 --> 00:45:59.056
I'm so sorry.


00:46:00.091 --> 00:46:01.468
How old was yours?


00:46:05.471 --> 00:46:06.472
Thirteen.


00:46:07.098 --> 00:46:08.020
God.


00:46:08.683 --> 00:46:09.855
That's awful.


00:46:11.686 --> 00:46:16.692
My son and my grandson
drowned four months ago.


00:46:17.775 --> 00:46:18.993
The little one was seven.


00:46:19.819 --> 00:46:20.946
Oh, my God!


00:46:22.071 --> 00:46:24.916
I've been coming here
for a couple of months now.


00:46:25.700 --> 00:46:27.293
And it has helped.


00:46:28.035 --> 00:46:30.629
It doesn't make it easier, obviously,


00:46:31.664 --> 00:46:34.634
but sometimes it makes it less lonely.


00:46:36.961 --> 00:46:37.962
Okay.


00:46:38.462 --> 00:46:41.181
And now I'm about to
embarrass myself, but, uh,


00:46:43.175 --> 00:46:44.552
if you need someone


00:46:46.470 --> 00:46:47.392
to talk to...


00:46:48.431 --> 00:46:49.523
'Cause we all do.


00:46:56.272 --> 00:46:57.148
If you need it.


00:47:00.318 --> 00:47:02.787
Okay.


00:47:03.279 --> 00:47:05.077
Thank you. Really.


00:47:08.200 --> 00:47:09.076
Okay.


00:47:14.040 --> 00:47:14.962
Bye-bye.


00:47:28.220 --> 00:47:29.312
- Hey.
- Hey.


00:47:31.098 --> 00:47:32.771
- I'm going to bed.
- Where were you?


00:47:33.559 --> 00:47:34.435
At the movies.


00:47:36.354 --> 00:47:37.230
Gonna go to bed.


00:47:37.480 --> 00:47:39.448
Okay. I'll come up with you.


00:47:40.358 --> 00:47:41.234
Okay.


00:48:01.712 --> 00:48:03.259
I'll be right back.


00:48:04.882 --> 00:48:06.976
No, you won't. You're taking the blanket.


00:48:08.344 --> 00:48:09.186
I can't sleep.


00:48:12.056 --> 00:48:13.228
It's freezing out there.


00:48:14.683 --> 00:48:15.855
Well, the heater's up there.


00:48:17.603 --> 00:48:18.479
Okay.


00:48:20.606 --> 00:48:21.573
Is that okay?


00:48:24.068 --> 00:48:25.536
If it gets too cold, come back in.


00:48:30.908 --> 00:48:31.955
I just need to sleep.


00:50:01.916 --> 00:50:02.758
Shit.


00:51:06.855 --> 00:51:08.903
Oh, Annie. You came.


00:51:08.983 --> 00:51:10.235
It's a little earlier than we said.


00:51:10.317 --> 00:51:12.570
Ah, you're perfect. Come in. Come in.


00:51:19.994 --> 00:51:22.122
Uh, your welcome mat.


00:51:22.746 --> 00:51:24.874
Ah! It's kind of cute, huh?


00:51:25.374 --> 00:51:27.627
Yeah. My mother used to
embroider ones just like that.


00:51:27.876 --> 00:51:29.753
Did she really? Isn't that funny?


00:51:31.130 --> 00:51:32.757
Please come in. Sit.


00:51:34.341 --> 00:51:35.433
First there's the...


00:51:37.428 --> 00:51:39.055
The smell of something wrong.


00:51:41.348 --> 00:51:42.190
And then...


00:51:43.767 --> 00:51:44.643
the body.


00:51:46.312 --> 00:51:51.819
Covered in black blood, like tar.


00:51:57.698 --> 00:52:00.497
And her head wasn't there,
so I couldn't see her face.


00:52:01.160 --> 00:52:03.458
But they were her clothes.


00:52:05.414 --> 00:52:08.634
And her hands, and her little fingernails.


00:52:44.536 --> 00:52:46.584
How is your relationship with your son?


00:52:48.207 --> 00:52:49.880
- Peter?
- Hmm.


00:52:51.585 --> 00:52:53.178
Oh, God. Um...


00:52:56.590 --> 00:52:57.842
Okay, I sleepwalk.


00:53:01.011 --> 00:53:03.309
I mean, I haven't done it in years,
but, um...


00:53:04.515 --> 00:53:07.018
A couple years ago, I woke up


00:53:08.018 --> 00:53:10.858
and I was standing next to Peter
in Charlie's bed


00:53:10.938 --> 00:53:13.942
when they shared a room.


00:53:16.527 --> 00:53:17.403
And they were


00:53:19.655 --> 00:53:22.079
completely covered in paint thinner.


00:53:24.076 --> 00:53:25.043
And so was I.


00:53:26.704 --> 00:53:27.751
From head to toe.


00:53:31.542 --> 00:53:34.296
And I was standing there
with a box of matches


00:53:34.378 --> 00:53:35.846
and an empty can of paint thinner.


00:53:38.549 --> 00:53:40.512
And I woke myself up striking the match,


00:53:40.592 --> 00:53:43.471
which also woke Peter up,
and he started to scream.


00:53:45.305 --> 00:53:49.026
- And I immediately put the match out.
- Like, immediately.


00:53:49.435 --> 00:53:51.813
I mean, I was just as shocked as he was.


00:53:53.564 --> 00:53:57.660
And it was impossible to convince them
that it was just sleepwalking,


00:53:58.360 --> 00:54:01.739
which of course it was, but...


00:54:02.990 --> 00:54:04.953
The timing was awful.


00:54:05.033 --> 00:54:07.956
Peter and I had gotten into
this stupid quarreling phase,


00:54:08.036 --> 00:54:10.664
just forever arguing about nothing, such...


00:54:13.584 --> 00:54:14.585
Frivolous stuff.


00:54:18.380 --> 00:54:20.132
And Peter always held it against me.


00:54:21.550 --> 00:54:24.178
And there is nothing I can say
and nothing I can do


00:54:25.512 --> 00:54:28.106
because it happened.


00:54:31.935 --> 00:54:32.936
While I was asleep.


00:54:37.983 --> 00:54:39.656
Hey! That was quick.


00:54:40.903 --> 00:54:42.246
Did you bike all the way here?


00:54:42.654 --> 00:54:44.577
Um, no. Actually, my friend drove me home.


00:54:44.948 --> 00:54:48.122
Oh, uh, by the way, Peter, have you, um...


00:54:48.202 --> 00:54:51.166
Have you signed up for that,
uh, SAT prep course?


00:54:51.246 --> 00:54:52.122
I'll do it tomorrow.


00:54:52.206 --> 00:54:54.834
Yeah, you know what, you gotta do that
because it's coming up.


00:55:31.495 --> 00:55:32.917
Jesus Christ, Annie.


00:55:34.623 --> 00:55:36.671
You're not planning on
letting him see that, are you?


00:55:37.167 --> 00:55:38.419
- Who?
- Peter.


00:55:38.877 --> 00:55:40.466
How do you think he's gonna feel
when he sees that?


00:55:40.546 --> 00:55:42.092
What? It's not about him.


00:55:42.172 --> 00:55:43.094
Oh, no?


00:55:43.549 --> 00:55:45.472
No. It's a neutral view of the accident.


00:55:55.602 --> 00:55:57.354
Are you, uh, are you coming down to dinner?


00:55:57.437 --> 00:55:58.358
I'm making dinner.


00:55:58.438 --> 00:55:59.940
No, I made the dinner. I came to get you.


00:56:00.524 --> 00:56:02.993
Come, stay, whatever you want.
I don't really give a shit.


00:56:50.657 --> 00:56:51.749
This is really good, Dad.


00:56:53.493 --> 00:56:54.415
Thanks, buddy.


00:57:13.972 --> 00:57:15.019
You okay, Mom?


00:57:19.186 --> 00:57:20.233
What?


00:57:22.522 --> 00:57:23.694
Is there something on your mind?


00:57:26.902 --> 00:57:28.370
Is there something on your mind?


00:57:31.490 --> 00:57:36.039
It just seems like there might be
something you wanna say.


00:57:36.119 --> 00:57:37.416
- Peter...
- Like what?


00:57:37.496 --> 00:57:41.421
I mean, why would I wanna say something
so I can watch you sneer at me?


00:57:43.043 --> 00:57:44.882
Sneer at you? I don't ever sneer at you.


00:57:44.962 --> 00:57:47.215
Oh, sweetie. You don't have to.
You get your point across.


00:57:47.839 --> 00:57:49.591
Okay, so, fine.
Then say what you wanna say, then.


00:57:49.675 --> 00:57:50.512
Peter.


00:57:50.592 --> 00:57:54.472
I don't wanna say anything.
I've tried saying things.


00:57:54.554 --> 00:57:56.476
Okay, so try again. Release yourself.


00:57:56.556 --> 00:57:57.853
Oh, release you, you mean.


00:57:57.933 --> 00:58:01.356
Yeah, fine. Release me. Just say it.
Just fucking say it!


00:58:01.436 --> 00:58:03.814
Don't you swear at me, you little shit!


00:58:03.897 --> 00:58:07.197
Don't you ever raise your voice at me!
I am your mother!


00:58:07.734 --> 00:58:08.781
Do you understand?


00:58:09.194 --> 00:58:13.285
All I do is worry and slave and defend you.


00:58:13.365 --> 00:58:16.744
And all I get back
is that fucking face on your face.


00:58:17.119 --> 00:58:22.210
So full of disdain and resentment
and always so annoyed.


00:58:22.290 --> 00:58:24.133
Well, now your sister is dead.


00:58:25.168 --> 00:58:28.133
And I know you miss her,
and I know it was an accident,


00:58:28.213 --> 00:58:29.676
and I know you're in pain.


00:58:29.756 --> 00:58:31.553
And I wish I could take that away for you.


00:58:31.633 --> 00:58:34.431
I wish I could shield you from the knowledge


00:58:34.511 --> 00:58:38.357
that you did what you did,
but your sister is dead!


00:58:39.057 --> 00:58:40.775
She's gone forever!


00:58:42.561 --> 00:58:44.279
And what a waste.


00:58:44.688 --> 00:58:47.277
If it could have maybe
brought us together or something.


00:58:47.357 --> 00:58:51.448
If you could have just said, "I'm sorry,"
or faced up to what happened.


00:58:51.528 --> 00:58:54.076
Maybe then we could do something with this.


00:58:54.156 --> 00:58:56.580
But you can't take responsibility
for anything!


00:58:56.950 --> 00:58:59.374
So now I can't accept...


00:58:59.828 --> 00:59:01.831
And I can't forgive,


00:59:02.998 --> 00:59:03.920
because...


00:59:06.501 --> 00:59:09.425
Because nobody admits anything they've done!


00:59:41.453 --> 00:59:42.500
What about you, Mom?


00:59:48.627 --> 00:59:49.924
She didn't wanna go to the party.


00:59:52.506 --> 00:59:53.598
So why was she there?


00:59:55.801 --> 00:59:58.099
All right. We're stopping this right now.


01:00:00.055 --> 01:00:00.931
That's it.


01:00:03.308 --> 01:00:05.982
I said stop right now.


01:00:06.478 --> 01:00:07.354
Fine!


01:00:15.403 --> 01:00:16.245
Fine.


01:01:30.061 --> 01:01:31.062
Joan?


01:01:32.314 --> 01:01:33.315
Oh!


01:01:33.899 --> 01:01:34.775
Annie!


01:01:34.858 --> 01:01:37.407
- Hi.
- Oh!


01:01:38.403 --> 01:01:39.871
- Annie!
- Hi!


01:01:41.573 --> 01:01:42.950
Oh, my!


01:01:43.491 --> 01:01:44.663
How are you?


01:01:45.160 --> 01:01:47.163
- Oh, Annie! I'm...
- Are you okay?


01:01:48.955 --> 01:01:53.336
I'm... I am, yes. I'm really good.


01:01:53.418 --> 01:01:54.920
I'm really, really...


01:01:55.420 --> 01:01:56.922
Okay.


01:01:58.340 --> 01:02:01.930
Something's... Something happened, Annie,


01:02:02.010 --> 01:02:06.106
and I feel completely turned around.


01:02:06.890 --> 01:02:08.733
What happened?


01:02:09.226 --> 01:02:10.853
I don't even know if I should say.


01:02:10.936 --> 01:02:12.063
What do you mean?


01:02:12.395 --> 01:02:14.067
You're gonna think I am crazy!


01:02:14.147 --> 01:02:15.274
No, not at all.


01:02:15.357 --> 01:02:17.325
Oh. Okay.


01:02:18.443 --> 01:02:19.410
All right, come on.


01:02:22.155 --> 01:02:23.077
I met...


01:02:24.449 --> 01:02:26.247
a spiritual medium.


01:02:28.078 --> 01:02:30.957
They were performing an open séance.


01:02:31.039 --> 01:02:34.384
I know, I know what you're thinking,
but they asked me to attend.


01:02:34.626 --> 01:02:37.254
They were bringing skeptics in,
and scientists.


01:02:37.337 --> 01:02:39.510
So I went, fully skeptical.


01:02:40.090 --> 01:02:42.013
And what I experienced there, Annie,


01:02:43.093 --> 01:02:44.220
was truly...


01:02:44.511 --> 01:02:45.512
Open séance.


01:02:45.595 --> 01:02:51.022
They brought in the spirit of a man
from the 19th century.


01:02:51.559 --> 01:02:55.358
And no, no, not in a kind of
smoke and mirrors way, no.


01:02:55.438 --> 01:02:59.779
And the man sitting next to me
was a completely cynical neurologist


01:02:59.859 --> 01:03:03.363
and he looked permanently changed
by the end of it.


01:03:04.239 --> 01:03:07.209
No, I... I...
I know what you're thinking. I do.


01:03:07.492 --> 01:03:10.962
But I... I approached the medium afterwards


01:03:11.204 --> 01:03:13.958
and I asked her about my son and my grandson


01:03:14.040 --> 01:03:16.794
and she came to my apartment and she...


01:03:22.632 --> 01:03:24.350
She ended up performing...


01:03:25.677 --> 01:03:26.519
Well...


01:03:28.179 --> 01:03:29.772
She conjured my grandson.


01:03:31.057 --> 01:03:33.980
No, no, no, I know,
I know what that smile is. I know.


01:03:34.060 --> 01:03:34.936
Annie, Annie...


01:03:35.437 --> 01:03:37.405
I wouldn't believe it either,
I didn't believe it,


01:03:38.398 --> 01:03:41.698
but I heard his voice.


01:03:42.652 --> 01:03:45.076
I felt his presence in the room.


01:03:45.405 --> 01:03:47.703
Annie, this is real.


01:03:49.617 --> 01:03:50.869
What are you doing right now?


01:03:51.828 --> 01:03:53.455
I'm just here shopping.


01:03:53.538 --> 01:03:54.505
Do you wanna come over?


01:03:55.123 --> 01:03:58.172
Oh, Annie. Please, Annie.
I really think you should.


01:03:58.501 --> 01:04:01.129
It would be everything if you came.


01:04:14.142 --> 01:04:15.394
Nice mood-setter.


01:04:25.737 --> 01:04:26.738
Okay.


01:04:28.740 --> 01:04:30.743
I'm going to put my hand on the glass...


01:04:32.410 --> 01:04:33.832
but I'm not going to add pressure.


01:04:35.413 --> 01:04:36.289
You do the same.


01:04:45.673 --> 01:04:46.515
All right.


01:04:52.472 --> 01:04:53.348
Louis...


01:04:56.434 --> 01:04:59.062
Louis, are you here? It's Grandma.


01:05:10.240 --> 01:05:11.162
Louis,


01:05:12.367 --> 01:05:13.994
if you are here with us,


01:05:15.620 --> 01:05:18.624
please just try and slide the glass.


01:05:23.461 --> 01:05:24.303
Louis,


01:05:26.047 --> 01:05:27.094
if you're here...


01:05:30.301 --> 01:05:31.223
Hi, Louis!


01:05:31.594 --> 01:05:34.723
- Hi, Louis!
- How did you do that?


01:05:36.057 --> 01:05:40.233
Louis, I'm going to ask you
some questions. Okay, sweetie?


01:05:40.854 --> 01:05:44.950
If the answer is yes,
slide the glass to the right.


01:05:45.608 --> 01:05:46.655
If it's no,


01:05:47.444 --> 01:05:50.243
slide it the other way, to the left.


01:05:50.655 --> 01:05:51.827
Do you understand?


01:05:55.743 --> 01:05:58.667
Louis, are you okay?


01:06:01.875 --> 01:06:03.093
Are you in pain?


01:06:04.669 --> 01:06:07.798
- Oh, my God!
- It's okay. It's okay.


01:06:08.381 --> 01:06:09.883
It's okay. It's okay.


01:06:10.216 --> 01:06:13.095
Louis, I brought your chalkboard.


01:06:13.678 --> 01:06:15.806
Remember your chalkboard?


01:06:17.640 --> 01:06:19.017
Can you write something?


01:06:47.837 --> 01:06:51.512
Oh, Louis! I love you, sweetheart!


01:06:52.175 --> 01:06:53.597
I'm sorry. Could we stop?


01:06:54.844 --> 01:06:55.932
What?


01:06:56.012 --> 01:06:57.514
I'm sorry. Please...


01:06:57.889 --> 01:07:01.814
Louis, we're going to stop for a second,
but I'll be right back.


01:07:06.105 --> 01:07:08.278
- Are you all right?
- I'm sorry, I'm just... I really...


01:07:08.358 --> 01:07:09.904
I understand, I understand.


01:07:09.984 --> 01:07:11.573
That's exactly how I reacted the first time.


01:07:11.653 --> 01:07:13.324
I have to go. Okay.
I'm... I'm sorry. Thank you.


01:07:13.404 --> 01:07:15.623
- No, no. It's okay. It's okay.
- Thank you. Yeah.


01:07:23.915 --> 01:07:26.543
I know. I know, honey.


01:07:26.626 --> 01:07:28.673
If you want to try this on your own...


01:07:28.753 --> 01:07:30.630
- God...
- It's okay. It's okay.


01:07:31.214 --> 01:07:32.682
First light the candle,


01:07:33.383 --> 01:07:35.977
then choose an item
that belonged to your daughter.


01:07:36.177 --> 01:07:38.975
That will be your link.
Mine was the chalkboard.


01:07:39.055 --> 01:07:40.102
That's my link.


01:07:40.682 --> 01:07:42.480
It's all right. It's all right.


01:07:42.809 --> 01:07:45.356
It's okay. There you go.


01:07:45.436 --> 01:07:46.654
Then when you're ready,


01:07:47.355 --> 01:07:49.232
read this out loud,


01:07:49.315 --> 01:07:52.069
every syllable, very carefully.


01:07:52.610 --> 01:07:54.533
Sorry, why? What is it?


01:07:54.862 --> 01:07:56.451
I don't know what language it is.


01:07:56.531 --> 01:07:58.578
The medium had me read it first.


01:07:58.658 --> 01:08:00.205
It's to make things start.


01:08:00.702 --> 01:08:03.166
But remember, your whole family...


01:08:03.246 --> 01:08:06.000
Every member needs to be in the house.


01:08:06.082 --> 01:08:08.836
Your son, everyone. Very important.


01:08:08.918 --> 01:08:10.045
- Okay.
- Okay?


01:08:10.878 --> 01:08:13.176
Deep breath.


01:08:13.256 --> 01:08:14.553
You didn't kill her, Annie.


01:08:20.471 --> 01:08:21.347
What?


01:08:22.056 --> 01:08:23.353
She isn't gone.


01:11:10.099 --> 01:11:10.941
Mom?


01:11:11.851 --> 01:11:12.727
What are you doing?


01:11:18.024 --> 01:11:19.025
What's going on?


01:11:20.651 --> 01:11:21.743
You're sleepwalking.


01:11:29.118 --> 01:11:29.960
I'm sorry.


01:11:31.621 --> 01:11:32.497
Is Charlie here?


01:11:35.708 --> 01:11:37.130
Why are you scared of me?


01:11:41.798 --> 01:11:42.720
What?


01:11:46.803 --> 01:11:48.100
I never wanted to be your mother.


01:11:53.601 --> 01:11:54.477
Why?


01:11:55.353 --> 01:11:56.320
I was scared.


01:11:58.856 --> 01:12:01.701
I didn't feel like a mother.


01:12:02.819 --> 01:12:03.911
But she pressured me.


01:12:05.446 --> 01:12:06.868
Then why did you have me?


01:12:06.948 --> 01:12:09.542
It wasn't my fault. I tried to stop it.


01:12:11.828 --> 01:12:12.829
How?


01:12:15.665 --> 01:12:17.212
I tried to have a miscarriage.


01:12:20.503 --> 01:12:21.470
How?


01:12:22.880 --> 01:12:23.718
However I could.


01:12:23.798 --> 01:12:26.677
I did everything they told me not to do,
but it didn't work.


01:12:27.593 --> 01:12:29.140
I'm happy it didn't work.


01:12:29.929 --> 01:12:31.556
You tried to kill me.


01:12:32.056 --> 01:12:33.102
No, I did not. I love you!


01:12:33.182 --> 01:12:34.645
You tried to kill me!


01:12:34.725 --> 01:12:36.814
- I love you!
- Why did you try to kill me?


01:12:36.894 --> 01:12:38.357
I didn't! I was trying to save you!


01:12:38.437 --> 01:12:40.026
Why did you try to kill me?


01:13:07.174 --> 01:13:08.175
Peter?


01:13:10.469 --> 01:13:11.846
Peter, sweetheart? Wake up.


01:13:11.929 --> 01:13:13.852
- What?
- It's okay. It's me.


01:13:14.181 --> 01:13:16.559
I am so, so sorry for everything.


01:13:16.642 --> 01:13:17.939
- Please, please forgive me.
- It's okay.


01:13:18.019 --> 01:13:19.315
I can't stand the things I said.


01:13:19.395 --> 01:13:20.271
It's okay. It's okay.


01:13:22.440 --> 01:13:24.443
Can you get up, sweetheart?
We're gonna try something.


01:13:24.859 --> 01:13:25.951
I was having a nightmare.


01:13:26.319 --> 01:13:27.740
Oh, it's okay. We can do something.


01:13:27.820 --> 01:13:28.696
Do what?


01:13:28.779 --> 01:13:30.497
I figured it out. Come on, come on.


01:13:32.992 --> 01:13:35.871
Steven. Baby. Steve, wake up.


01:13:37.371 --> 01:13:38.584
- What?
- Come downstairs.


01:13:38.664 --> 01:13:39.882
We're gonna try something together.


01:13:40.249 --> 01:13:41.125
Come on, come on.


01:13:44.629 --> 01:13:45.716
Steve, come on. Let's go.


01:14:00.728 --> 01:14:02.150
- Dad?
- It's okay.


01:14:10.529 --> 01:14:11.781
Come on, come on!


01:14:18.371 --> 01:14:19.293
Okay.


01:14:19.956 --> 01:14:21.003
So...


01:14:21.248 --> 01:14:22.716
It's freezing in here.


01:14:23.209 --> 01:14:24.797
Wait! No, no, no. What are you doing? Wait!


01:14:24.877 --> 01:14:27.174
- I'm gonna close the window.
- No, no. We can't change anything.


01:14:27.254 --> 01:14:28.426
I don't wanna mess it up.


01:14:29.006 --> 01:14:30.758
Everyone needs to sit. Come sit.


01:14:32.051 --> 01:14:33.639
My friend Joan taught me how to do this.


01:14:33.719 --> 01:14:35.938
What friend Joan?


01:14:36.514 --> 01:14:39.478
We need our palms on the table
and our fingers to touch. Please.


01:14:39.558 --> 01:14:41.060
What are we doing here, Annie?


01:14:41.143 --> 01:14:42.235
Please. You'll see.


01:14:44.563 --> 01:14:45.439
Please.


01:14:46.440 --> 01:14:47.441
Trust me.


01:14:51.070 --> 01:14:52.242
All right, fine.


01:14:56.242 --> 01:14:58.040
We can do it over here then.


01:14:58.995 --> 01:15:01.089
Peter. Okay.


01:15:02.498 --> 01:15:04.501
Okay, Steve. Come on.


01:15:05.876 --> 01:15:07.253
I need you both to concentrate.


01:15:07.545 --> 01:15:08.507
On what?


01:15:08.587 --> 01:15:10.176
Think about Charlie, if you can.


01:15:10.256 --> 01:15:11.677
- Oh, for fuck's sake.
- Sweetheart, please.


01:15:11.757 --> 01:15:14.010
- I tried this 20 minutes ago and it worked.
- What worked?


01:15:14.093 --> 01:15:15.470
I would not bring you down here if it didn't.


01:15:15.553 --> 01:15:17.146
- Well, I just need to show you.
- Show what?


01:15:17.888 --> 01:15:19.686
Fuck! I'm a...


01:15:20.433 --> 01:15:21.646
I'm a medium, okay?


01:15:21.726 --> 01:15:25.192
I was seeing apparitions earlier and I
just shook them off and I shouldn't have.


01:15:25.521 --> 01:15:27.944
Please, I know how it sounds,
but there's no way to talk about it.


01:15:28.024 --> 01:15:29.820
I just need to show you, okay?
Please, you'll see.


01:15:29.900 --> 01:15:31.652
- I'm completely lucid.
- Peter, go to bed.


01:15:31.736 --> 01:15:34.740
What! No, no, no! Peter, please!
We need to do this as a family.


01:15:34.822 --> 01:15:37.200
This needs all our energies, okay? Together.


01:15:37.450 --> 01:15:39.418
All right, I'll stay.


01:15:40.161 --> 01:15:41.707
Steve. Steve, please.


01:15:41.787 --> 01:15:44.085
I really, really need you to be open to this.


01:15:44.165 --> 01:15:46.963
Please, please. I promise... Both of you.


01:15:47.043 --> 01:15:49.467
Please. I need you to be open. Please.


01:15:50.087 --> 01:15:51.430
Come on, Steve. Come on, come on.


01:15:52.840 --> 01:15:53.807
I promise.


01:15:54.592 --> 01:15:57.061
Okay.


01:15:57.678 --> 01:15:58.520
Okay, good.


01:15:59.430 --> 01:16:02.730
So, I read that earlier.
I don't think I need to read that again.


01:16:03.934 --> 01:16:05.652
What language is even that?


01:16:06.437 --> 01:16:08.656
Try to concentrate.


01:16:15.613 --> 01:16:16.535
Charlie?


01:16:18.407 --> 01:16:19.750
Charlie, are you here?


01:16:28.042 --> 01:16:29.169
Charlie, it's Mommy.


01:16:30.711 --> 01:16:32.008
And Daddy and Peter.


01:16:39.386 --> 01:16:43.936
Charlie, if you're in this room with us,
I'm gonna have us all touch the glass.


01:16:44.016 --> 01:16:45.268
Don't add pressure.


01:16:46.685 --> 01:16:50.030
Now, if you're in here, Charlie,
I want you to move the glass for us.


01:16:50.564 --> 01:16:52.361
- Even if it's just a tiny bit.
- Oh, Jesus Christ, Annie!


01:16:52.441 --> 01:16:54.489
Even if it's just the tiniest
little movement. Okay, Charlie?


01:16:56.779 --> 01:16:57.826
Okay.


01:16:59.198 --> 01:17:00.040
Shit.


01:17:01.700 --> 01:17:02.701
What the hell?


01:17:03.786 --> 01:17:05.163
- What?
- You don't feel that?


01:17:06.122 --> 01:17:07.123
What? Feel what?


01:17:07.206 --> 01:17:10.710
Like, you don't feel the air flexing?


01:17:14.505 --> 01:17:16.552
Wow! Yes!


01:17:16.632 --> 01:17:18.555
Thank you, Charlie! That was so good!


01:17:19.135 --> 01:17:22.514
Okay. Now, Charlie,
what I'd like for you to do


01:17:22.596 --> 01:17:25.190
is I'd like for you to show them
what you did earlier.


01:17:29.687 --> 01:17:31.233
Can you show them
what you just did for me before?


01:17:31.313 --> 01:17:33.156
- Mom.
- She's gonna do it.


01:17:38.195 --> 01:17:40.242
- That's enough.
- What? No, no, no!


01:17:40.322 --> 01:17:42.290
Listen, when I did this earlier,


01:17:43.033 --> 01:17:45.752
this manifested on the page. I saw it!


01:17:46.162 --> 01:17:47.333
- I saw it!
- What is it?


01:17:47.413 --> 01:17:48.790
- It's Charlie!
- Annie!


01:17:48.873 --> 01:17:50.294
Charlie, did you want to draw some more?


01:17:50.374 --> 01:17:52.001
- You can keep going.
- Stop it! Stop it!


01:17:52.084 --> 01:17:53.506
Okay, we need to keep our fingers touching...


01:17:53.586 --> 01:17:55.758
You are scaring him!


01:17:55.838 --> 01:17:57.761
No, I am not! Peter, Peter, listen...


01:17:58.465 --> 01:17:59.466
Stop it!


01:17:59.550 --> 01:18:01.678
Listen to me. There is no need to be scared.


01:18:01.760 --> 01:18:02.978
This is your sister.


01:18:04.471 --> 01:18:05.438
Mom.


01:18:08.309 --> 01:18:10.858
Charlie, what's wrong?


01:18:51.310 --> 01:18:52.357
Hello?


01:18:53.270 --> 01:18:54.647
- Mom?
- Mom?


01:18:56.190 --> 01:18:57.533
- Mom?
- I don't like this.


01:18:57.816 --> 01:18:58.654
Dad, I don't like this.


01:18:58.734 --> 01:18:59.947
- What's happening?
- Please stop.


01:19:00.027 --> 01:19:01.740
- Annie, please, stop this.
- What's going on?


01:19:01.820 --> 01:19:03.033
- Mom!
- Please.


01:19:03.113 --> 01:19:04.831
You're really freaking me out. Please stop.


01:19:04.949 --> 01:19:07.452
- What's happening? Why is everyone scared?
- Dad, make it stop.


01:19:07.785 --> 01:19:09.537
Why are you scaring me!


01:19:09.620 --> 01:19:11.623
Make it stop! Make it fucking stop!


01:19:11.705 --> 01:19:13.794
- Make it stop!
- Where's Mom?


01:19:13.874 --> 01:19:16.672
Stop it! Stop it now! Please stop!


01:19:16.752 --> 01:19:19.176
- Mom? Peter? Peter, I'm scared.
- Dad, make it stop!


01:19:20.589 --> 01:19:24.219
What the hell? What are you doing?


01:19:33.227 --> 01:19:34.069
What happened?


01:20:19.189 --> 01:20:21.487
Our country has had many ups and downs,


01:20:21.567 --> 01:20:23.155
economically speaking.


01:20:23.235 --> 01:20:25.954
We've talked about the struggles
during the 1800s


01:20:26.363 --> 01:20:29.082
compared to the fall of 1929,


01:20:29.616 --> 01:20:33.792
in an era that become known appropriately
as the Great Depression.


01:20:34.371 --> 01:20:37.750
For a decade, we suffered
through many, many hardships.


01:20:38.125 --> 01:20:43.050
In 1929, Wall Street had been going so well


01:20:43.130 --> 01:20:46.680
that when it finally crashed
because of the Great Boom,


01:20:46.967 --> 01:20:51.558
it caused a huge decline in the economy.


01:20:51.638 --> 01:20:54.858
So much so that it caused food lines.


01:20:57.936 --> 01:21:02.237
This is where the Federal Government has,
or still has...


01:21:13.494 --> 01:21:15.582
Uh, uh. Yes, Peter?


01:21:15.662 --> 01:21:18.040
Um, I'm sorry. I have to go to the bathroom.


01:21:18.332 --> 01:21:20.710
Um, of course. Take the pass.


01:21:24.546 --> 01:21:25.513
As I was saying...


01:21:31.387 --> 01:21:32.434
Hello?


01:21:32.721 --> 01:21:34.348
<i>Can you guess who just called me from school</i>


01:21:34.431 --> 01:21:36.058
<i>in complete hysterics?</i>


01:21:37.518 --> 01:21:38.394
Charlie?


01:21:38.977 --> 01:21:39.819
<i>What?</i>


01:21:41.355 --> 01:21:43.483
Uh, nothing. What happened?


01:21:43.565 --> 01:21:47.031
<i>Peter just called me, Annie,
terrified, crying in the halls,</i>


01:21:47.111 --> 01:21:50.490
<i>convinced he's being threatened
by some vengeful spirit.</i>


01:21:50.739 --> 01:21:52.457
Why does he think he's being threatened?


01:21:52.908 --> 01:21:55.411
<i>Listen to me, Annie. I have a son to protect.</i>


01:21:56.370 --> 01:21:57.207
What does that mean?


01:21:57.287 --> 01:21:59.585
<i>It means that that's what
I'm worried about right now</i>


01:21:59.665 --> 01:22:00.502
<i>and that's how...</i>


01:22:00.582 --> 01:22:01.834
Hey, don't talk to me like this.


01:22:01.917 --> 01:22:03.169
He's my son too...


01:22:03.585 --> 01:22:04.507
Oh!


01:22:15.264 --> 01:22:17.562
Do not hang up on me again.


01:22:17.766 --> 01:22:20.986
I am not sleepwalking anymore.
Do you understand?


01:22:46.378 --> 01:22:49.097
<i>At the tone,
please record your voice message.</i>


01:22:49.423 --> 01:22:50.969
<i>When you are finished recording,</i>


01:22:51.049 --> 01:22:53.768
<i>you may hang up or press pound
for more options.</i>


01:22:54.011 --> 01:22:55.888
<i>Annie, hi!</i>


01:22:55.971 --> 01:22:58.099
<i>This is Patrick at the Archer Gallery.</i>


01:22:58.182 --> 01:23:01.311
<i>Um, I was just calling
first to see how you're doing,</i>


01:23:01.602 --> 01:23:02.945
<i>how your family's doing.</i>


01:23:03.353 --> 01:23:07.194
<i>We've all been thinking about you
and just worrying about you</i>


01:23:07.274 --> 01:23:08.651
<i>and hoping you're okay.</i>


01:23:08.901 --> 01:23:11.120
<i>You guys have been
in our constant thoughts and prayers.</i>


01:23:11.445 --> 01:23:16.662
<i>And then also, uh,
we just wanted to, well, to say first,</i>


01:23:16.742 --> 01:23:19.120
<i>if you need us to postpone the show
or push the date,</i>


01:23:19.620 --> 01:23:20.963
<i>it's obviously more than okay.</i>


01:23:21.622 --> 01:23:25.712
<i>And if not, uh, we just wanna call and see</i>


01:23:25.792 --> 01:23:28.637
<i>if we could help in any way or offer...</i>


01:23:40.891 --> 01:23:43.269
Oh, jeez. That smell.


01:23:53.111 --> 01:23:55.114
Annie? What's that smell?


01:24:20.639 --> 01:24:21.731
What the fuck happened here?


01:24:23.225 --> 01:24:25.102
I didn't feel like looking at it anymore.


01:27:14.146 --> 01:27:15.068
Charlie?


01:27:55.520 --> 01:27:57.648
Peter? Oh, my God, Peter!


01:27:59.024 --> 01:28:00.570
What's wrong, baby? What's happening?


01:28:00.650 --> 01:28:01.526
What are you doing?


01:28:01.610 --> 01:28:02.486
What do you mean?


01:28:02.569 --> 01:28:04.116
You were pulling on my head!


01:28:04.196 --> 01:28:07.826
What? No, I wasn't. I just came in.
You were screaming. What happened?


01:28:07.908 --> 01:28:09.285
I saw Charlie in the corner


01:28:09.367 --> 01:28:11.331
and then you started
trying to pull my head off!


01:28:11.411 --> 01:28:14.835
Oh, Peter. I would never do that to you.
Are you crazy? Please, baby.


01:28:16.291 --> 01:28:17.463
What corner did you see Charlie?


01:28:19.628 --> 01:28:20.924
Peter, listen to me.


01:28:21.004 --> 01:28:22.968
I don't know what's happening
or what you just saw,


01:28:23.048 --> 01:28:24.391
but I am stopping this.


01:28:24.841 --> 01:28:26.888
Do not tell Dad what you just said to me.


01:28:26.968 --> 01:28:28.682
Do not, okay? Because it is not true.


01:28:28.762 --> 01:28:31.015
Something is happening
and I'm the only one who could stop it.


01:28:31.097 --> 01:28:33.851
Do you understand?
I'm the only one who can fix this.


01:31:15.929 --> 01:31:16.930
Joan?


01:31:21.935 --> 01:31:23.653
Joan, please. I need to talk to you.


01:31:27.649 --> 01:31:29.822
Joan, I really need to ask you a question.


01:31:37.742 --> 01:31:38.709
Joan!


01:32:01.975 --> 01:32:03.522
Peter!


01:32:09.024 --> 01:32:09.991
Peter!


01:32:12.485 --> 01:32:14.112
Peter!


01:32:18.366 --> 01:32:20.414
I expel you!


01:32:24.414 --> 01:32:26.007
Zantany!


01:32:31.087 --> 01:32:32.430
Dagdany!


01:32:35.008 --> 01:32:36.430
Aparagon!


01:32:39.179 --> 01:32:40.476
Peter!


01:32:41.139 --> 01:32:44.063
Get out!


01:32:48.480 --> 01:32:49.902
Peter!


01:33:17.425 --> 01:33:18.347
Oh, God.


01:36:50.513 --> 01:36:53.107
...so everyone feels justified.


01:36:55.226 --> 01:36:58.321
Iphigenia's murder was commanded by the gods.


01:37:29.719 --> 01:37:31.813
So, really, Agamemnon had no choice...


01:38:00.750 --> 01:38:01.672
Peter.


01:38:04.128 --> 01:38:05.050
Peter, what's wrong?


01:38:08.383 --> 01:38:09.976
Peter, are you all right?


01:38:16.015 --> 01:38:18.188
Can he breathe?


01:38:18.684 --> 01:38:19.685
Peter, what are you doing, man?


01:39:01.853 --> 01:39:04.072
<i>Call from West High School.</i>


01:39:24.292 --> 01:39:25.464
Hello.


01:39:26.794 --> 01:39:27.716
Yes, it is.


01:40:06.709 --> 01:40:08.882
Oh, thank God.


01:40:10.254 --> 01:40:12.677
Wait, what? Oh, my God!


01:40:12.757 --> 01:40:15.260
What happened? What happened to him?


01:40:15.343 --> 01:40:17.515
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.


01:40:17.595 --> 01:40:21.190
Oh, my God. Oh, no. Oh, who did that?


01:40:21.390 --> 01:40:22.983
He did it, apparently, to himself.


01:40:25.561 --> 01:40:27.108
Smashed his face into his own desk.


01:40:27.188 --> 01:40:29.652
Okay, Steve. Wait, wait. Wait, Steve. Listen.


01:40:29.732 --> 01:40:32.030
Take his feet. Please, take his feet.


01:40:37.990 --> 01:40:40.955
Steve, uh, upstairs...


01:40:41.035 --> 01:40:44.959
In the attic, when you were gone,
I went up there and I...


01:40:45.039 --> 01:40:47.667
I just... I really need you
to go up there and see what I saw.


01:40:49.043 --> 01:40:50.340
There's a body.


01:40:51.671 --> 01:40:53.259
Yeah. I mean, I think it's my mother,


01:40:53.339 --> 01:40:55.091
I think, but I can't tell
because the skin's all black


01:40:55.174 --> 01:40:57.302
and she's all distended,
but the head is gone.


01:40:58.928 --> 01:41:01.352
Will you, please? I just need you
to go and see upstairs.


01:41:03.849 --> 01:41:05.726
Please, Steve.


01:41:17.697 --> 01:41:18.698
And then there's more.


01:41:19.907 --> 01:41:22.410
You mean more than
your mother's headless body?


01:41:22.702 --> 01:41:23.669
Of course there is.


01:42:12.001 --> 01:42:13.844
- Jesus, fuck!
- Okay, there's more.


01:42:14.128 --> 01:42:15.346
What the fuck was that?


01:42:15.880 --> 01:42:17.132
Why didn't you call the police?


01:42:17.214 --> 01:42:18.341
The police can't help us.


01:42:19.383 --> 01:42:20.304
Who the fuck is that up there?


01:42:20.384 --> 01:42:22.598
Do you remember Joan,
my friend whose grandson died?


01:42:22.678 --> 01:42:25.017
- She took me to her apartment.
- It did look like your mother.


01:42:25.097 --> 01:42:26.849
Well, listen.
She taught me how to do the séance.


01:42:26.932 --> 01:42:29.272
I didn't even want to,
but she brought her grandson back


01:42:29.352 --> 01:42:31.320
and I saw it and felt it
just like you did with Charlie.


01:42:31.562 --> 01:42:34.657
Now, look. This is my mother's album.
Now look here.


01:42:35.066 --> 01:42:37.820
See this? See her? That's her. That's Joan.


01:42:37.902 --> 01:42:39.404
She didn't even mention knowing my mom


01:42:39.487 --> 01:42:41.200
and I've never met her before,
but she approached me.


01:42:41.280 --> 01:42:42.493
She consoled me.


01:42:42.573 --> 01:42:44.701
She told me about this séance,
and she showed me how.


01:42:44.784 --> 01:42:46.998
Now look at this. See this symbol?
On the necklace my mom gave me.


01:42:47.078 --> 01:42:47.915
It's her necklace, right?


01:42:47.995 --> 01:42:50.874
They're both wearing it,
and they're wearing it in every photo.


01:42:50.956 --> 01:42:52.878
And look at that pattern!
Did you see up there?


01:42:52.958 --> 01:42:55.423
This was painted above the body, right?


01:42:55.503 --> 01:42:56.550
In blood!


01:42:58.089 --> 01:42:59.136
You dug up the grave.


01:43:00.508 --> 01:43:01.721
It was you, wasn't it?


01:43:01.801 --> 01:43:02.638
What?


01:43:02.718 --> 01:43:04.971
All those nights you were pretending
to go to the movies.


01:43:05.054 --> 01:43:06.142
You're not even listening!


01:43:06.222 --> 01:43:07.810
And then the day the cemetery called, I said,


01:43:07.890 --> 01:43:10.187
"Oh, I won't tell her
because she'd be worried."


01:43:10.267 --> 01:43:12.106
Oh, God damn it! Listen to me, Steve!


01:43:12.186 --> 01:43:15.531
I know you don't trust me
and there is nothing I can do about that.


01:43:16.482 --> 01:43:18.860
But they put a curse on us
when we brought Charlie back.


01:43:18.943 --> 01:43:20.656
We made a pact with something.


01:43:20.736 --> 01:43:21.782
Something that is in this house.


01:43:21.862 --> 01:43:23.614
I don't know what it is,
but it is after Peter.


01:43:23.698 --> 01:43:26.452
I watched these pages fill.


01:43:26.534 --> 01:43:28.878
All of them are Peter!


01:43:29.620 --> 01:43:31.709
I'm sorry. I don't know what I did.


01:43:31.789 --> 01:43:34.292
I don't know what I did,
but Peter is in danger.


01:43:35.126 --> 01:43:36.503
And I started it.


01:43:37.753 --> 01:43:39.221
Now, if we destroy this book,


01:43:40.256 --> 01:43:41.553
it will take me too.


01:43:43.175 --> 01:43:44.347
I tried to burn it. I tried.


01:43:44.427 --> 01:43:48.014
But my arm caught on fire on its own as if I
was linked to it because I am linked to it.


01:43:48.097 --> 01:43:50.395
I understand this now. Please!


01:43:51.142 --> 01:43:52.860
If we don't destroy this book...


01:43:56.188 --> 01:43:57.440
Peter will...


01:43:59.316 --> 01:44:01.694
Oh, God. Do you understand?


01:44:03.404 --> 01:44:07.453
We have to do this.
Please, please, please, please.


01:44:07.533 --> 01:44:08.534
For Peter.


01:44:20.463 --> 01:44:22.215
I need you to trust me, Steve.


01:44:24.258 --> 01:44:27.137
It needs to be me. It's my fault.


01:44:27.470 --> 01:44:30.098
It's my fault. I know it's my fault. Please.


01:44:30.848 --> 01:44:33.693
Please, I need you to throw it in the fire.


01:44:35.102 --> 01:44:36.229
Please, I just... I can't do it.


01:44:36.312 --> 01:44:40.237
I can't. I'm just too fucking scared.
But if we don't do it...


01:44:40.816 --> 01:44:44.490
If we don't do it, it's gonna be Peter,
it's gonna be our son.


01:44:44.570 --> 01:44:46.823
Okay, I know this. I know so.


01:44:46.906 --> 01:44:50.536
Just, please, please,
please, please, please...


01:44:54.872 --> 01:44:57.545
Steve, please. Please understand, baby.


01:44:57.625 --> 01:45:01.630
Please, please. Please throw it in the fire.


01:45:10.304 --> 01:45:11.601
Sweetheart, please.


01:45:12.598 --> 01:45:14.937
Please take it, take it. You gotta do it.


01:45:15.017 --> 01:45:16.269
You gotta do it.


01:45:16.352 --> 01:45:18.190
Okay. Thank you, thank you.


01:45:18.270 --> 01:45:19.613
Okay, here.


01:45:21.190 --> 01:45:22.403
Okay.


01:45:22.483 --> 01:45:24.076
Now listen to me. Listen to me.


01:45:31.826 --> 01:45:35.501
Oh! You are the love of my life.


01:45:41.001 --> 01:45:44.176
I love you, Steve. I love you so, so much.


01:45:45.464 --> 01:45:47.512
Oh, God, I love you so much.


01:45:47.925 --> 01:45:49.677
And I love Peter so much.


01:45:54.265 --> 01:45:55.357
Now please, just...


01:45:57.226 --> 01:45:58.444
Please just throw it in.


01:46:17.037 --> 01:46:19.005
I'm not gonna do this with you anymore.


01:46:20.040 --> 01:46:21.758
What? No, no, no!


01:46:22.084 --> 01:46:24.132
No, no, it's not helpful for you.


01:46:25.129 --> 01:46:27.348
You are sick, Annie.


01:46:28.465 --> 01:46:29.842
I need to call the police.


01:46:31.176 --> 01:46:32.598
Oh, God!


01:47:40.204 --> 01:47:41.046
Mom?


01:47:45.042 --> 01:47:45.918
Dad?


01:49:23.182 --> 01:49:24.104
Mom?


01:49:25.476 --> 01:49:26.352
Dad?


01:49:52.628 --> 01:49:53.675
Hello?


01:50:41.927 --> 01:50:42.928
Mom?


01:53:22.754 --> 01:53:24.927
Stop! Mom, please stop!


01:53:25.340 --> 01:53:27.763
Mom, I'm sorry! Okay, I'm sorry.


01:53:31.722 --> 01:53:34.895
Mommy. Mommy, please. I'm begging you.


01:53:34.975 --> 01:53:36.193
I'm begging you to stop.


01:53:45.068 --> 01:53:45.990
Mommy?


01:55:03.188 --> 01:55:05.360
Just gotta wake up.


01:55:05.440 --> 01:55:07.317
You just gotta wake up. Come on. You're okay.


01:55:07.401 --> 01:55:10.405
Just wake up. Wake up! Wake up! Wake up!


02:01:27.197 --> 02:01:29.040
Oh, hey, hey, hey.


02:01:30.033 --> 02:01:31.034
It's all right.


02:01:32.118 --> 02:01:33.040
Charlie...


02:01:37.332 --> 02:01:38.629
You're all right now.


02:01:41.795 --> 02:01:42.637
You...


02:01:44.130 --> 02:01:45.382
are Paimon,


02:01:46.800 --> 02:01:49.474
one of the eight kings of Hell.


02:01:52.514 --> 02:01:56.895
We have looked to the Northwest
and called you in.


02:01:58.102 --> 02:02:00.901
We've corrected your first female body


02:02:01.481 --> 02:02:05.577
and give you now this healthy male host.


02:02:06.736 --> 02:02:12.084
We reject the Trinity
and pray devoutly to you, great Paimon.


02:02:12.826 --> 02:02:16.706
Give us your knowledge of all secret things.


02:02:17.288 --> 02:02:21.794
Bring us honor, wealth, and good familiars.


02:02:22.627 --> 02:02:25.381
Bind all men to our will,


02:02:25.713 --> 02:02:31.391
as we have bound ourselves
for now and ever to yours.


02:02:38.935 --> 02:02:40.357
Hail, Paimon!


02:02:41.437 --> 02:02:43.565
Hail, Paimon!


02:02:45.024 --> 02:02:47.322
Hail, Paimon!


02:02:48.695 --> 02:02:50.538
Hail!

